# --- Generated, and deliberately NOT ignored ---------------------------
# schemas/, examples/, redcorpus/, runs/good/ and ledger/ (the fixture chain)
# are all committed on purpose. They are reproducible from their generators,
# and CI regenerates them and diffs against what is committed. That diff is a
# real check: it proves the corpora in the repo are the ones the generators
# actually produce, not hand-edited artifacts that drifted.
#
# The demo append timestamp is pinned for exactly this reason. With a live
# clock the fixture ledger head moved every build, cascading into every
# example's ledger_ref, so a committed tree showed spurious diffs constantly —
# which trains everyone to ignore diffs, which is how a real one gets through.

# --- Genuinely non-reproducible ---------------------------------------
# A real emitted run carries a fresh run_id, wall-clock timestamps, and the
# live ledger head. It SHOULD differ every time; that is what makes it a
# record rather than a fixture. Committing it would produce noise and imply a
# single run is canonical when the point is that anyone can produce their own.
runs/real/

# Release artifacts belong on the Releases page, not in the tree.
*.tar.gz
*.whl
*.zip

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-release/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

